# Garden — Cursor AI Context Document

> This file provides Cursor AI with full context about the Garden project —
> its architecture, design system, data flow, and customization points.
> Read this before making any changes.

---

## Project Overview

**Garden** is a personal dashboard ("Your Personal OS") built with Next.js 15 (App Router).
It aggregates live stock data, RSS articles, news headlines, and financial goals into a
single beautiful page styled with a "Botanical Minimalism" aesthetic. Built for Caleb, a
23-year-old graphic designer who freelances and is exploring starting his own business.

This is a **Next.js 15** project using the App Router, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS 3.
It fetches live data from Yahoo Finance and RSS feeds via server-side API routes, with
all user customization stored in localStorage via a shared preferences hook.

---

## Architecture

```
app/
├── layout.tsx              → Root layout with Google Fonts (Instrument Sans, Cutive)
├── globals.css             → Design tokens, @font-face for OPTI Century, Tailwind layers
├── page.tsx                → Main Garden dashboard (client component, reads preferences)
├── hooks/
│   └── usePreferences.ts   → Shared preferences hook (localStorage persistence)
├── preferences/
│   └── page.tsx            → Preferences editor page (name, tickers, feeds, goals)
├── api/
│   ├── stocks/route.ts     → Yahoo Finance stock quotes via yahoo-finance2
│   ├── feeds/route.ts      → RSS articles + news (GET defaults, POST custom feeds)
│   └── growth/route.ts     → Plaid-ready placeholder for bank data
public/
├── fonts/                  → OPTI Century Expanded Two font files:
│   ├── OPTI-Century-Expanded-Two.woff2.otf (primary)
│   ├── OPTI-Century-Expanded-Two.otf (fallback copy)
│   └── README.md (font usage docs)
└── garden/                 → Nature photography assets (5 images)
```

### Data Flow

1. **Client** (`page.tsx`) reads user preferences from `usePreferences()` hook
2. **Client** calls `/api/stocks` (GET with tickers) and `/api/feeds` (POST with custom feeds)
3. **Server** API routes fetch from Yahoo Finance and RSS feeds
4. **Client** renders live data with loading/error states and graceful fallbacks
5. **Growth section** reads goals directly from localStorage preferences

