## API Routes

### GET /api/stocks

**Query params:** `tickers` (comma-separated, e.g., NVDA,AVGO,GOOGL)

**Returns:** `StockQuote[]`
```ts
{
  ticker: string;      // "NVDA"
  title: string;       // "NVIDIA Corporation"
  price: number;       // 135.42
  change: number;      // 2.67
  changePercent: string; // "+2.01%"
  direction: "up" | "down";
  source: string;      // "NMS — USD"
}
```

**Package:** `yahoo-finance2` — calls `yahooFinance.quote(ticker)`

### POST /api/feeds

**Body:** `{ type: "articles" | "news", limit?: number, feeds: { url: string, name: string }[] }`

Also supports GET with defaults: `GET /api/feeds?type=articles&limit=8`

**Returns for type=articles:** `Article[]`
```ts
{
  id: string;
  title: string;
  author: string;
  duration: string;    // "around 8 min."
  url: string;
  publishedAt: string; // ISO date
  source: "substack";
}
```

**Returns for type=news:** `NewsHeadline[]`
```ts
{
  id: string;
  title: string;
  summary: string;     // First 200 chars of content
  source: string;      // "NYT", "BBC", "CNN", "Wired"
  url: string;
  publishedAt: string;
}
```

**Package:** `rss-parser` — fetches and parses RSS/XML feeds

### GET/POST /api/growth

**Plaid-ready placeholder.** Currently returns `{ connected: false, goals: [] }`.
The frontend reads goals from localStorage instead. See "Future Integration: Plaid" below.

---

## User Preferences System

All preferences are stored in localStorage under key `garden:preferences:v1`.

### Schema (`GardenPreferences`)
```ts
{
  displayName: string;           // Greeting name (default: "caleb")
  tickers: string[];             // Stock ticker symbols
  substackFeeds: SubstackFeed[]; // { url, name }
  newsFeeds: NewsFeed[];         // { url, name }
  growthGoals: GrowthGoal[];     // { id, name, targetAmount, currentAmount }
}
```

### Hook: `usePreferences()`
- Located at `app/hooks/usePreferences.ts`
- Returns `{ preferences, updatePreferences, loaded, DEFAULT_PREFERENCES }`
- `updatePreferences(partial)` merges and persists to localStorage
- Used by both `page.tsx` (reading) and `preferences/page.tsx` (editing)

### Other localStorage Keys

| Key | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| `garden:preferences:v1` | Full user preferences object (JSON) |
| `garden:seeds-complete:v1` | JSON array of ticker IDs (lowercase) marked as "read" |

Note: The active index (stream/seeds/winds/growth) is tracked via IntersectionObserver — NOT persisted.

---

## Mobile Responsiveness

The layout uses a mobile-first approach with these key responsive behaviors:

| Element | Mobile (< 640px) | Desktop (≥ 768px) |
|---------|-------------------|---------------------|
| Hero title | `clamp(3.5rem, 16vw, 12rem)` | Same (fluid) |
| Index Switcher | 140×140px, centered | 190×190px, right-aligned |
| Seeds section | Full-width, no forest image | 2-col with forest image |
| Growth cards | Stacked vertically | Horizontal with side image |
| Winds section | Single column, no middle image | 3-column grid |
| Section titles | 36px | 52px → 68px |
| Footer links | Centered, stacked | Row, space-between |
| Stream articles | Single column | 2-column grid |

---

## How to Customize

### Via Preferences Page (`/preferences`)
- **Display name** — changes the greeting
- **Stock tickers** — add/remove ticker symbols
- **Substack feeds** — add/remove RSS feed URLs with display names
- **News feeds** — add/remove news outlet RSS URLs
- **Growth goals** — add/remove/edit financial goals with targets and current amounts

### Via Code
- **Add a new section**: Add `GardenIndex` type value, create JSX with id/ref, add to IndexSwitcher
- **Change images**: Replace files in `public/garden/` and update `IMG` object in `page.tsx`
- **Change fonts**: Update `layout.tsx` Google Fonts imports and `globals.css` @font-face
- **Change colors**: Update the hex values in component classNames (no CSS variables used)

---

## Future Integration: Plaid (Bank Sync)

The `/api/growth` route is a placeholder for Plaid integration. To implement:

1. `npm install plaid`
2. Set environment variables: `PLAID_CLIENT_ID`, `PLAID_SECRET`, `PLAID_ENV`
3. Create `/api/plaid/link-token` — generates a Link token for Plaid Link
4. Create `/api/plaid/exchange` — exchanges public_token for access_token
5. Store access_token securely (encrypted localStorage or a database)
6. Update `/api/growth` to call `plaid.accountsBalanceGet()` and map to goals
7. Update `GrowthSection` to show real balances alongside manual goals

---

## Running the Project

```bash
# Install dependencies
npm install

# Start development server (Turbopack)
npm run dev

# Build for production
npm run build

# Serve production build
npm start

# Lint
npm run lint
```

The dev server runs at `http://localhost:3000` by default.

---

## Key Dependencies

| Package | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `next` ^15.1.0 | React framework with App Router |
| `react` ^19.0.0 | UI library |
| `tailwindcss` ^3.4.16 | Utility-first CSS |
| `yahoo-finance2` ^2.14.0 | Live stock quotes from Yahoo Finance |
| `rss-parser` ^3.13.0 | Parse RSS/Atom feeds |

---

## Deployment Notes

- **Vercel** (recommended): Zero-config Next.js deployment. API routes run as serverless functions.
- **Railway/Render**: Works with `npm run build && npm start`
- **Self-hosted**: Standard Node.js server via `next start`

No environment variables are required — the app uses public APIs (Yahoo Finance, public RSS feeds).

